  "slug": "gentius",
  "summary": "Gentius was the last attested Illyrian king, ruling from 181 to 168 BC from Scodra, in present-day Albania. Initially allied with Rome, he switched sides in 169 BC and joined Perseus of Macedon. In 168 BC, Roman forces under Lucius Anicius Gallus defeated him at Scodra. Gentius surrendered, was taken captive to Rome, and later held at Iguvium. Rome divided his former kingdom into three administrative districts, ending the Ardiaean state’s independence. The date of Gentius’s death is unknown.",
